  "title": "Susan La Flesche Picotte",
  "summary": "Susan La Flesche Picotte, born on the Omaha Reservation in Nebraska in 1865, graduated from the Woman's Medical College of Pennsylvania in 1889 and became the first American Indian woman to receive a medical degree. She served as physician to the Omaha people and opened a reservation hospital in 1913. She died in Walthill, Nebraska, in 1915.",
